BT /F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.0 790.0 Tm (READING PASSAGE 3) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.0 771.1 Tm (You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 27–40, which are based on Reading Passage 3 below.) Tj ET
BT /F2 16 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.0 750.6 Tm (The Case for City Trees) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.0 724.6 Tm (City planners have long treated trees as decoration: pleasant to look at, but the first thing to be cut) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.0 708.7 Tm (when a budget is reduced. I believe this attitude is a serious mistake. A growing body of research) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.0 692.7 Tm (shows that trees are among the cheapest and most effective tools a city has for protecting the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.0 676.8 Tm (health of its people.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.0 651.8 Tm (The clearest benefit is shade. On a summer afternoon, a street lined with mature trees can be up) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.0 635.9 Tm (to ten degrees cooler than a bare one. As heatwaves become more frequent, this difference is not) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.0 619.9 Tm (a matter of comfort but of survival, especially for older residents. Air conditioning can cool a single) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.0 604.0 Tm (building, but only trees can cool an entire neighbourhood without using electricity.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.0 579.0 Tm (Trees also reduce flooding. Their roots allow rainwater to soak into the ground instead of running) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.0 563.1 Tm (across concrete into drains, and their leaves catch a surprising amount of rain before it reaches the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.0 547.1 Tm (ground. Some engineers argue that new drainage pipes are a better investment, but pipes must be) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.0 531.2 Tm (replaced every few decades, while a well-chosen tree can live for a century or more.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.0 506.2 Tm (The effect on mental health is harder to measure, yet it may be the most important of all. Studies in) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.0 490.3 Tm (several countries have found that people who can see trees from their windows report lower levels) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.0 474.3 Tm (of stress. Hospital patients with a view of greenery have even been reported to recover more) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.0 458.4 Tm (quickly, although I suspect the size of this effect has sometimes been exaggerated.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.0 433.4 Tm (None of this means that any tree in any place will do. A species that needs a great deal of water) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.0 417.5 Tm (may die in a dry summer, and roots planted too close to buildings can damage foundations. Cities) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.0 401.5 Tm (therefore need trained specialists who can choose the right tree for each street. Such experts are) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.0 385.6 Tm (rare, and in my view training more of them should be a priority for every local council.) Tj ET
endstream
